  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Meda Hanumantharao Hanumanthu, vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh, on 4 February, 2020 Author: J. Uma Devi Bench: J. Uma Devi The Hon'Ble Ms. Justice J. Uma Devi Criminal Petition No.597 Of 2020 Order:",
    "facts": "2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 14.12.2019 at about 6-00 PM near Lachannagudi village of Tadikonda mandal, the complainant along with his staff on credible information seized the auto bearing No.AP 07 TE 6340 and caught hold the petitioners/A.1 to A.3, seized the banned products under a cover of police proceedings and arrested the petitioners/A.1 to A.3. Later, he registered the mediators report as a case in Crime No.207 of 2019 for the offences stated supra.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
